WEBVTT

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:19.820
I activate the trap card Wave Rebound!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Incredible!  All the gods are destroyed!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.010
Team Ragnarok's Harald takes damage equal 
to the three gods' total attack points!

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.870
Team 5D's has made a 
come-from-behind victory!

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:37.650
Good, Yusei!

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.600
That's what you had to do!

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.870
Show all your strategies to the gods!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.540
What are you thinking?

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.330
I activate a trap from the graveyard!

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.320
A trap from the graveyard?

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.050
Gjallarhorn unleashes its effect 
when it's in the graveyard.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:13.130
When Asgard's guard Heimdallr blows 
Gjallarhorn, the final war Ragnarok begins.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.530
Yusei, this duel is almost over.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.680
This trap will bury you!

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.800
Though you tried to use Wave Rebound to make 
a comeback, Gjallarhorn's effect negates it!

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:35.720
Gjallarhorn negates effects that 
try to stop the gods' resurrection.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:39.780
At the End Phase of my third 
turn, all monsters on my field

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:45.210
are removed from play, and you take damage 
equal to their total attack points!

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.190
What?

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:51.380
Team Ragnarok has their gods on their 
field during the End Phase of every turn.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.800
This card is the gods' final weapon!

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.290
The three Aesir's total 
attack points are 10800!

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.160
In three turns, Yusei will take it as damage!

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.410
Oh no!  Yusei's strategy 
is completely overturned!

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.520
Yusei...

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:15.040
When Thor, Lord of the Aesir resurrects, 
Thor deals 800 points of damage!

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:24.490
When Loki resurrects, I can add one 
trap card in my graveyard to my hand.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:28.930
I return the trap card Odin's Eye to my hand!

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.200
Next...

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.170
We'll finally win.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.910
Once Gjallarhorn activates, 
no one has ever survived.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:43.720
How long will Yusei survive 
during these three turns?

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.670
Due to the resurrected Odin's effect, 
I draw one card from my deck.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.780
I end my turn.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.380
The Continuous Trap Gjallarhorn's 
counter becomes 1.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.790
Yusei, it's the countdown 
to your destruction.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.270
The trap card Monster Chain's 
effect vanishes this turn.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.330
Now bring it, Yusei Fudo!

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.310
Riding Duels.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.360
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:25.230
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:46.500
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:56.580
Soar in the infinite skies   BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:02.820
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:08.790
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:14.570
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:20.170
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:26.540
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:32.320
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:38.620
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:44.960
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:15.030
Gjallarhorn!Countdown to Death

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.020
Unbelievable!

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:22.300
Team 5D's Yusei Fudo counterattacked with 
everything he had, but it's all for naught!

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:27.800
What will Team 5D's Yusei Fudo 
do against the three gods?

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.250
He read my entire hand.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:39.610
As long as he has Odin's Eye in his hand...

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:45.800
When a god is on the field, you 
can't negate Odin's Eye's effect.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:56.040
Once per turn, I can negate the gods' effects to 
either look at one of your set cards or your hand!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.600
I can still make a comeback!

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:01.840
It has a weakness because it's all-knowing!

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:05.390
My turn!

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.880
I summon Stardust Phantom!

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.110
When this card is destroyed 
and sent to the graveyard,

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:20.640
I can Special Summon Stardust Dragon 
from my graveyard in defense position.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.260
And if I remove Stardust Phantom 
in my graveyard from play...

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:27.910
...Stardust Dragon gains 
an effect where it won't be

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.240
destroyed in battle by lowering 
its defense points by 800.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.630
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.810
So that's your plan.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.290
God's authority shines 
to the ends of the earth,

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:43.580
but since Stardust Phantom's effect 
activates from the graveyard,

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.610
Thor can't negate it.

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:52.530
And if all three gods attack, he'll survive by 
resurrecting Stardust Dragon from the graveyard.

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:55.150
Stardust Dragon has 2000 defense points.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:59.500
If he uses Stardust Phantom's 
effect, he can survive

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.560
three attacks from the gods and 
still keep Stardust Dragon.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.110
But you forgot one strategy.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.890
I'll have 10 Speed Counters on the next turn!

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.620
My turn!

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.720
I activate Speed World 2's effect.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:22.930
I remove 10 Speed Counters to 
destroy one card on the field!

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.250
I destroy Stardust Phantom!

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.680
Stardust Phantom's effect activates!

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.520
When this card is destroyed 
and sent to the graveyard,

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.130
I can Special Summon Stardust 
Dragon from my graveyard!

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.160
Go, Thor!

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.120
I activate Stardust Phantom's effect!

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.710
By removing this card in 
my graveyard from play,

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:53.780
Stardust Dragon loses 800 defense 
points and isn't destroyed in battle!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.030
Thunder Pyle!

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.920
Go, Loki!

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.120
Vanity Bullet!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.230
I activate Stardust Phantom's effect again!

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.910
But it's over for you.  
Stardust Dragon doesn't have

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:24.890
enough defense points left to 
use Stardust Phantom's effect!

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.370
You were one move short, Yusei.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.310
Go, Odin!

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:32.330
Don't leave Stardust Dragon on the field!

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.620
Heaven's Judgment!

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.060
I activate Stronghold Guardian's effect!

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:54.180
When my monster in defense 
position is attacked, it gains

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:59.850
1500 defense points until the End Phase 
by sending this card to the graveyard!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.310
Stardust Phantom's effect activates!

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:03.290
What?

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.700
I'm sorry, Stardust Dragon.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.600
He survived the gods' attacks?

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:17.680
Yusei, your resilience scares me.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.660
So I'll be extra careful.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:25.880
I Special Summon Jörmungardr the 
Nordic Serpent on your field!

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.230
What's this?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.900
What's this monster?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:42.670
When a god is on my field, 
I can Special Summon

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:46.070
Jörmungardr from my hand to 
your field in defense position.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:52.710
When Jörmungardr switches to attack 
position, you take 3000 points of damage.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:57.500
Next, I activate the trap card 
Gleipnir, the Fetters of Fenrir.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:04.200
When a god is on my field, I can add Fenrir 
the Nordic Wolf from my deck to my hand.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.420
When a god is on the field, 
I can Special Summon

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:11.020
this card from my hand to your 
field in defense position.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.500
I Special Summon Fenrir on your field!

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:19.860
When it becomes the Battle Phase, this card

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:23.650
switches all your monsters in defense 
position to attack position.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:29.690
And when this card battles, both 
players take battle damage!

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:30.640
What?

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.080
What an unbelievable combo card!

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.820
What combo?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:38.100
When it's the Battle Phase 
of Yusei's next turn,

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.610
Fenrir switches his monsters from 
defense position to attack position.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:47.820
In other words, Jörmungardr switches to attack 
position, and Yusei takes 3000 points of damage.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:48.650
No way!

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:49.310
It can't be!

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:52.320
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:56.500
Gjallarhorn now has 2 counters!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:04.310
This is bad!  Gjallarhorn 
also has 2 counters!

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:05.200
Yusei!

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:11.170
More importantly, Yusei can't attack if he 
doesn't do something about Jörmungardr and Fenrir.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.130
The card he set is Odin's Eye.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.710
My turn!

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.250
I activate the trap Hope for Escape!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:31.080
When I have fewer life points than 
you, I can pay 1000 life points

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:35.870
to draw one card for every 1000-point 
difference in our life points!

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.220
Our life points differ by over 3000 points!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.060
Therefore, I draw three cards!

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:47.620
Whoa!  Yusei Fudo is taking a huge risk!

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:50.740
He intentionally reduced his 
own life points to draw cards!

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:53.470
He only has 200 life points left!

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:57.820
Yusei intentionally went 
below the safety line!

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.060
Oh no!

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:00.690
It's fine.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.490
Harald only has 1 Speed Counter.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.450
He can't activate an effect that 
will take away Yusei's life points.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:11.360
Yeah.  Gjallarhorn's effect will 
activate on Harald's next turn.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:14.770
That means Yusei only has one turn left!

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.840
I summon Life Gardna!

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:45.550
Next, I can Special Summon this card by 
removing one monster on my field from play!

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.700
I remove Jörmungardr from play to Special 
Summon Different Dimension Sprite!

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:54.550
What?

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:57.930
Nice!  He used Jörmungardr to his advantage!

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:01.010
Fenrir and Jörmungardr's combo is gone!

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:06.120
Level 1 Different Dimension Sprite 
tunes Level 1 Life Gardna!

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:10.370
The wishes come together to 
invite a new world of speed!

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.180
Become the path that lights the way!

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.800
Synchro Summon!

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:17.960
The Synchro Tuner with the power 
of hope!  Formula Synchron!

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.940
Synchro Tuner?

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.550
Will he Accel Synchro?

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:24.150
I activate Life Gardna's effect!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:28.640
When I use this card as Synchro 
Material, I regain 800 life points!

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.760
Then I activate Formula Synchron's effect!

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.190
Once per turn, I can draw 
one card from my deck!

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.350
The key to my duel lies within speed!

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:47.200
The place I reached is Clear Mind!

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:51.540
Yusei is going to do it!

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:58.950
Level 2 Formula Synchron tunes Level 
8 Synchro Monster Stardust Dragon!

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:07.290
Dreams crystallize to open 
a new door of evolution!

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.980
Become the path that lights the way!

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.510
Accel Synchro!

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.410
He vanished!

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:26.900
Arise!  Shooting Star Dragon!

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.440
Shooting Star Dragon!

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:35.680
He played his ace!

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:39.480
I activate Speed Spell - 
Star Force from my hand!

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:45.360
When I have 4 or more Speed Counters, by 
removing a monster on my field from play...

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.960
...a monster gains attack 
points equal to the removed

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:52.100
monster's Level multiplied by 
100 points until the End Phase!

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:54.350
I remove Fenrir from play!

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:08.240
Fenrir is Level 10, so Shooting Star 
Dragon gains 1000 attack points!

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:10.910
4300 attack points?

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.450
He even used Fenrir to his advantage!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:15.560
Shooting Star Dragon's effect activates!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.940
Once per turn, I look at 
the top 5 cards in my deck.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.390
Shooting Star Dragon can attack for 
every Tuner Monster that I draw!

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:27.200
I drew three Tuners.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.100
Therefore, it can attack three times!

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.080
Go, Shooting Star Dragon!

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.020
Stardust Mirage!

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.730
I'm being overwhelmed?

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.440
Oh no!  He won't make it!

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:15.120
He doesn't have enough attacks.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.360
Yusei Fudo, you're incredible.

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:27.520
If you drew just one more Tuner 
Monster, I would've lost.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:31.710
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:36.060
The three gods resurrect 
during this turn's End Phase!

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:44.460
When Thor resurrects, you 
take 800 points of damage!

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.120
Yusei!

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:53.370
Yusei is back to 200 life points.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:59.040
When Loki resurrects, I can add a trap 
card from my graveyard to my hand.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:03.760
I add Gleipnir, the Fetters of Fenrir 
from my graveyard to my hand.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:10.830
When Odin resurrects, I 
draw one card from my deck.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:15.620
And Shooting Star Dragon's 
attack points return to normal!

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:19.950
My turn!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.070
This is incredible!

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:27.860
Yusei Fudo and Harald are 
having an incredible battle!

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:31.940
Even though Yusei Fudo is 
our enemy, he's impressive.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:34.880
He's done well against the three Aesir.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.820
But Harald is still going to win.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.530
Gjallarhorn will activate 
during the End Phase.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:43.360
Yusei has two set cards on his field.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:46.010
Everything depends on those cards!

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:53.980
There's now only one key to win this duel.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:55.930
Bring it, Harald!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.740
You're still not giving up?

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:03.420
I told you that I won't 
give up until the very end!

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:06.740
Yusei, you're counting on 
your two set cards to make

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:11.430
a comeback, but you're forgetting 
something important.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:14.310
My god Odin is almighty!

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:17.710
It reveals all your strategies!

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.150
Let's battle!

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:25.840
We'll see who'll win!  Our gods 
or your evolved Synchro Monster!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.920
I summon Tyr of the Nordic Champions!

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:40.650
I activate the trap card Odin's Eye!

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.550
It's that card again!

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:46.100
He'll be able to read Yusei's hand!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:52.300
When a god is on the field, you can't 
negate Odin's Eye's activation.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:59.750
By negating my gods' effects this turn, I can 
either look at one of your set cards or your hand!

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:02.360
I activate Tyr's effect!

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:08.580
I release Tyr to negate spell, trap 
and monster effects against my gods.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:13.690
My gods won't suffer a drawback 
for using Odin's Eye!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.520
Harald's field is now safe.

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:21.200
I use Odin's Eye and select that card!

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:25.670
I was waiting for this moment!

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.460
I activate my trap Trick Mirror!

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:35.080
When your trap card activates, its 
effect activates as if it's mine!

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.570
I copy Odin's Eye's effect!

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:46.800
What?

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:50.710
Therefore, your gods' 
effects are still negated!

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:55.020
Even though Odin doesn't have its effects, 
it still has 4000 attack points!

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:59.280
It's more than Shooting Star 
Dragon's 3300 attack points!

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.930
Go, Odin, Father of the Aesir!

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:06.460
Shooting Star Dragon's effect activates!

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:13.160
By removing Shooting Star Dragon from play 
during your turn, your monster's attack is negated!

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:17.050
But your field is now empty!

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:20.290
I still have two gods that can attack!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:23.490
The trap card Zero Force!

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:27.310
When my monster leaves the 
field, all other monsters

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:31.270
that have equal or greater attack 
points now have 0 attack points!

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:32.530
What?

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.350
The gods have 0 attack points!

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.240
They can't attack!

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:45.230
At this turn's End Phase, the Continuous 
Trap Gjallarhorn's effect activates!

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:50.390
Gjallarhorn's effect removes all 
monsters on your field from play,

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:54.110
and I take damage equal to 
their total attack points.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:58.040
But your three gods have 0 attack points!

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.170
Therefore, I take 0 damage!

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:02.880
